#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 4917..5865
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/5
msgid ""
"It might be good to start out by studying its\n"
"movements,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 5879..6617
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/6
msgid ""
"watching what it does before each attack.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 6645..7202
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/7
msgid ""
"That should help you avoid most of them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 7230..8400
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/8
msgid ""
"And weapons that walk always have one\n"
"guaranteed weakness.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 8428..8735
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/9
msgid ""
"The legs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 8749..9933
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/10
msgid ""
"Right. Destroy its legs and you'll stop it from\n"
"moving.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 9961..10797
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/11
msgid ""
"You might even be able to knock it on its back if\n"
"you're lucky.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_mis_amd0190_000_0
#. timeline 10825..11661
#: codec/1/206/0xce6b0/12
msgid ""
"Just make sure you're out the way first.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/0
msgid ""
"Snake, you have to stop the launch! It's going to\n"
"strike Cuba!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/1
msgid ""
"I know, I know!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/2
msgid ""
"The situation has changed completely now that it\n"
"has been upgraded.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/3
msgid ""
"I do not know if your old tactics will work.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/4
msgid ""
"But the basic strategy remains the same.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/5
msgid ""
"Try to anticipate what it's going to do before it\n"
"does it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/6
msgid ""
"So, you probably won't have as much time to stand\n"
"around staring.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/206/0xcec00/7
msgid ""
"Wasn't counting on it. I'll manage somehow.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/207/0xcf360/0
msgid ""
"Sabotaging enemy bases is another principle of\n"
"guerilla warfare.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/207/0xcf360/1
msgid ""
"You will need explosives for that,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/207/0xcf360/2
msgid ""
"and naturally once they detonate the enemy will\n"
"know you're there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/207/0xcf360/3
msgid ""
"So you need to make sure you have enough time\n"
"to get to safety before they go off.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/207/0xcf360/4
msgid ""
"Best to plan your escape route before you go and\n"
"plant the explosives.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/207/0xcf5a0/0
msgid ""
"You could always use those.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/207/0xcf650/0
msgid ""
"Sometimes the enemy will respond to guerilla\n"
"activity with numbers.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/207/0xcf650/1
msgid ""
"Under no circumstances should you engage the\n"
"enemy in this situation.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/207/0xcf650/2
msgid ""
"Focus on staying calm, carefully studying enemy\n"
"movement, and staying out of sight.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/207/0xcf650/3
msgid ""
"You must also be careful not to make any noise\n"
"that would attract attention, of course.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/207/0xcf650/4
msgid ""
"Likewise, it is important to listen for any noises the\n"
"enemy makes to get a fix on their position.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/207/0xcf650/5
msgid ""
"Do not forget to check for signs of the enemy\n"
"other than sight and sound.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/207/0xcf650/6
msgid ""
"To check for signs of the enemy, do <I=ESEARCH> when\n"
"you're pressed against a wall or prone.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 445..2006
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/0
msgid ""
"The supply staging point is at the eastern foot of\n"
"Irazú. There's a rail terminal there -\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 2089..3009
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/1
msgid ""
"they'll probably transfer the nuke from the train\n"
"onto a truck.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 3037..3928
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/2
msgid ""
"Gotcha. I'll have to catch them while they're moving\n"
"the cargo.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 3956..5057
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/3
msgid ""
"But you might run into el basilisco... Keep your\n"
"eyes peeled, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 5113..6394
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/4
msgid ""
"An 80-foot-tall walking behemoth... The CIA's new\n"
"weapon?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 6520..7453
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/5
msgid ""
"Could be. Too bad it's not actually a dinosaur.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 7718..8749
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/6
msgid ""
"I think they're testing it up at the base on top of\n"
"the mountain.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 8763..9445
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/7
msgid ""
"I met a guy in Russia who described it as\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 9557..10407
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/8
msgid ""
"\"a metal gear linking infantry and artillery...\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 10421..10741
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/9
msgid ""
"Metal gear...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 11201..11828
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/10
msgid ""
"I've got a bad feeling about this.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 11981..12859
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/11
msgid ""
"Like maybe it's connected to everything that's\n"
"happening here somehow.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 12901..13806
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/12
msgid ""
"The nukes? You don't think...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 13834..15353
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/13
msgid ""
"...What else could it be? If it is up there, I'll just\n"
"have to improvise.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 15422..16202
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/14
msgid ""
"Either way, I won't know until I get there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0050_000_0
#. timeline 16244..16676
#: codec/1/207/0xcf9d0/15
msgid ""
"Watch your back, Snake...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 445..1184
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/0
msgid ""
"So there's a real basilisco that lives in the river?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 1184..2326
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/1
msgid ""
"I'm only saying I heard stories from people who\n"
"said they saw it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 2410..3650
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/2
msgid ""
"But I know lots of places to find it in Nicaragua.\n"
"You wanna go have a look?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 3678..4263
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/3
msgid ""
"I don't have time for sightseeing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 4611..4987
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/4
msgid ""
"You don't like lizards?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 5015..5962
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/5
msgid ""
"It's not that. I just think snakes taste better.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 5976..6422
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/6
msgid ""
"...Who said anything about taste?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 6492..7007
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/7
msgid ""
"How about you? You like 'em?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 7007..8791
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/8
msgid ""
"Not that way... they do look kinda like dinosaurs,\n"
"though. You don't think that's cool?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 8944..10170
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/9
msgid ""
"They're both reptiles, yeah. But there's a big\n"
"difference size-wise.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 10170..11006
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/10
msgid ""
"I'll bet there are still big ones around somewhere.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 11089..12385
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/11
msgid ""
"They say mammals multiplied and ate up their\n"
"eggs, but they can't all be gone.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 12469..13026
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/12
msgid ""
"They've gotta exist somewhere out there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 13625..14001
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/13
msgid ""
"Dinosaur eggs, huh...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 14029..14586
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/14
msgid ""
"And animals are always evolving, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 14698..15757
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/15
msgid ""
"Maybe they evolved so much they don't even look\n"
"like dinosaurs anymore.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 15770..16592
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/16
msgid ""
"Then you can't really call them dinosaurs, can you?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0060_010_0
#. timeline 16620..18362
#: codec/1/208/0xd04a0/17
msgid ""
"I guess not... Yeah, you're right, dinosaurs've gotta\n"
"be big!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_000_0
#. timeline 431..1630
#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/0
msgid ""
"Irazú has more than one crater, 'cause it's erupted\n"
"so many times.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_000_0
#. timeline 1671..2758
#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/1
msgid ""
"I heard most of them filled up with rainwater and\n"
"became lakes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_000_0
#. timeline 27439..44878
#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/2
msgid ""
"Calderas, huh.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/3
msgid ""
"Calderas? Yeah, something like that.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/4
msgid ""
"...Hey, I got an idea.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/5
msgid ""
"When you get to the lake, can you keep an eye out\n"
"for weird animals for me?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/6
msgid ""
"People all over the world tell stories about giant\n"
"monsters living in lakes.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/7
msgid ""
"Nessie in Loch Ness, Nahuelito in Argentina,\n"
"Ogopogo in Canada...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/8
msgid ""
"I can hardly keep track of them all.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/9
msgid ""
"They say that all these sightings prove dinosaurs\n"
"do still exist.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/10
msgid ""
"But crater lakes are isolated. They're not\n"
"connected to rivers.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/11
msgid ""
"Yeah, but... you know Mokèlé-mbèmbé? In the\n"
"Congo River? He can walk on land.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/12
msgid ""
"So maybe they moved there from some other lake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/13
msgid ""
"You sure know a lot about UMAs.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/14
msgid ""
"There used to be a guy in el Frente who was a\n"
"hunter. He taught me lots of things.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/15
msgid ""
"He even said he once went to a place called Isla\n"
"del Monstruo.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/16
msgid ""
"A hunter on Isla del Monstruo...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/17
msgid ""
"Someday, I'm gonna be a hunter and catch some\n"
"rare animals.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/208/0xd0ae0/18
msgid ""
"Right after we restore peace to our land, of course.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 459..1030
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/0
msgid ""
"You ever hear of the Loch Ness Monster?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 1044..2187
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/1
msgid ""
"Now that one I know. Pretty much everyone's\n"
"heard of ol' Nessie.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 2215..3859
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/2
msgid ""
"Great, so I don't have to explain. I think she's a\n"
"long-lost dinosaur, don't you?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 3887..4611
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/3
msgid ""
"Uh, sure, why not.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 4625..5503
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/4
msgid ""
"One of the compas gave me a book about it - with\n"
"photos.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 5558..6199
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/5
msgid ""
"It looks exactly like the plesiosaur.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 6227..6840
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/6
msgid ""
"...Then why does it only live in Loch Ness?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 6854..7509
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/7
msgid ""
"Well it probably got cut off from the ocean.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 7592..8178
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/8
msgid ""
"Back when Loch Ness was part of the ocean,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 8219..9111
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/9
msgid ""
"some plesiosaurs became trapped there when the\n"
"climate changed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 9195..10086
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/10
msgid ""
"There weren't any mammals there, so no natural\n"
"predators.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 10156..11048
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/11
msgid ""
"Today's Nessie is descended from those\n"
"plesiosaurs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 11048..12594
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/12
msgid ""
"Then... wouldn't it make sense for there to be\n"
"monsters in other lakes with similar climates?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 12608..13987
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/13
msgid ""
"Exactly! That's why there's been giant monster\n"
"sightings in a bunch of other places\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 14029..14879
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/14
msgid ""
"- like Nahuelito and Ogopogo.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 14949..15575
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/15
msgid ""
"I don't know if there's one in Irazú, too...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_010_0
#. timeline 15617..16620
#: codec/1/209/0xd11a0/16
msgid ""
"But I know there's definitely something living in\n"
"Lago Cocibolca.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 445..1365
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/0
msgid ""
"You mentioned the Nahuelito... What is it?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 1365..3204
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/1
msgid ""
"It's a plesiosaur that lives in Lago Nahuel Huapi in\n"
"Argentina. It's described a little differently,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 3232..4931
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/2
msgid ""
"but I'm sure it's basically the same creature as\n"
"Nessie. Except for one thing...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 5099..6784
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/4
msgid ""
"Well, according to one theory, it's the result of a\n"
"nuclear test back in the '50s...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 6826..7969
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/5
msgid ""
"What? There's no record of a nuclear test in\n"
"Argentina in the '50s.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 8024..8860
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/6
msgid ""
"At the time the president, General Juan Peron,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 8874..9585
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/7
msgid ""
"was pushing hard to industrialize the country.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 9696..10630
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/8
msgid ""
"I wouldn't be surprised if he conducted a\n"
"top-secret nuclear test\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 10685..11187
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/9
msgid ""
"before he was overthrown in a coup.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 11521..12190
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/10
msgid ""
"Sounds a little far-fetched to me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 12204..13555
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/11
msgid ""
"You think? Then maybe Nahuelito really is a\n"
"dinosaur.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 13583..14043
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/12
msgid ""
"No, I didn't say...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 14071..14795
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/13
msgid ""
"I mean, it's really pretty obvious...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 14837..15018
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/14
msgid ""
"Wait a...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 15130..15631
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/15
msgid ""
"Thanks for clearing that up, Boss!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_020_0
#. timeline 15659..16272
#: codec/1/209/0xd17b0/16
msgid ""
"... dinosaur...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 445..2048
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/0
msgid ""
"Mokèlé-mbèmbé lives in the Congo River. There's\n"
"nothing mysterious about it, though\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 2089..3051
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/1
msgid ""
"- it's already been confirmed as a real, living\n"
"dinosaur.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 3120..4402
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/2
msgid ""
"The local people know all about it, and when they\n"
"were shown a drawing of a brontosaurus,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 4458..5280
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/3
msgid ""
"every one of them said it was Mokèlé-mbèmbé.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 5405..6534
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/4
msgid ""
"When peace returns to Nicaragua, I wanna go to\n"
"the Congo myself...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 6798..7746
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/5
msgid ""
"...The revolutionary movement in the Congo ended\n"
"in failure, you know.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 7760..9348
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/6
msgid ""
"Yeah, I know. I wish we could do something to help,\n"
"but Africa's awfully far away.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 9376..9585
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/7
msgid ""
"Africa...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 9626..10421
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/8
msgid ""
"I wonder if El Che ever saw Mokèlé-mbèmbé...?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 10476..10853
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/9
msgid ""
"I wonder if I will...?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 11173..12106
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/10
msgid ""
"Best to take care of business here before\n"
"daydreaming about Africa.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0070_040_0
#. timeline 12134..12775
#: codec/1/210/0xd21a0/11
msgid ""
"Yeah, I guess you're right...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/1
msgid ""
"You know much about cloud forests?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/2
msgid ""
"Not that much... All I know is\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/3
msgid ""
"there's a world of difference between a rainy rain\n"
"forest and a foggy cloud forest.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/4
msgid ""
"But they have some things in common...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/5
msgid ""
"Like for instance you gotta watch out for poison\n"
"dart frogs.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/6
msgid ""
"Both rain and cloud forests have high humidity,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/7
msgid ""
"so they're perfect environments for frogs and\n"
"other amphibians.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/8
msgid ""
"I mean, it's not like just touching a strawberry\n"
"poison dart frog or\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/9
msgid ""
"a dyeing dart frog is going to kill you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/10
msgid ""
"But don't eat 'em, no matter how hungry you get.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/11
msgid ""
"I can get all the rations I need from Mother Base.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/12
msgid ""
"No jungle food for me this time.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/13
msgid ""
"Seriously? You're not disappointed you don't get to\n"
"eat wild animals?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/14
msgid ""
"...What do you think I am?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/15
msgid ""
"Ha ha ha. Just kidding. In Colombia, though, there's\n"
"a frog\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/16
msgid ""
"- the golden dart frog - that's lethal to the touch.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/17
msgid ""
"How do you know all this?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/18
msgid ""
"C'mon, don't you think poisonous animals are cool?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/19
msgid ""
"Not if you get poisoned by one.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/20
msgid ""
"Well, obviously. One more thing.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/21
msgid ""
"When you get to the forest, be on the lookout for\n"
"Bigfoot.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/210/0xd2620/22
msgid ""
"I... think I'll be OK there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 459..1393
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/0
msgid ""
"Gotta admit, I've never heard of Mono Grande.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 1407..2814
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/1
msgid ""
"Yeah, he's not as famous as Bigfoot. He's similar,\n"
"but he lives in Venezuela.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 2856..3622
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/2
msgid ""
"He's not that big - less than two vara (5.5 ft)\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 3678..4374
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/3
msgid ""
"- but he's way more ferocious than Bigfoot.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 4820..6199
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/4
msgid ""
"I wonder just how mean he is? Like when he\n"
"catches his prey, does he punch it to death...?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 6213..7941
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/5
msgid ""
"That's the law of the wild: you catch your prey,\n"
"you kill it, and you eat it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 7955..8888
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/6
msgid ""
"Yeah! Yeah! But punching is way more ferocious\n"
"than biting.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 9083..10017
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/7
msgid ""
"Maybe it seems that way because that's what\n"
"humans do.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 10044..10783
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/8
msgid ""
"...You really love UMAs, don't you, Chico?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 10811..11953
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/9
msgid ""
"You know what I think? I think UMAs should be\n"
"dangerous.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0080_020_0
#. timeline 12037..12775
#: codec/1/211/0xd3310/10
msgid ""
"Otherwise where's the fun in hunting them?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/0
msgid ""
"Did you see a quetzal, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/1
msgid ""
"Yep.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/2
msgid ""
"What do you think? Did it look like a snake?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/3
msgid ""
"Huh? No, it didn't look like a snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/4
msgid ""
"Oh, really? ...Must be different from the\n"
"quetzalcoatl, then.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/5
msgid ""
"Quetzalcoatl?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/6
msgid ""
"A winged snake from Mayan and Aztec legend.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/7
msgid ""
"A winged snake...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/8
msgid ""
"Weird, right? I bet it's a UMA.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/9
msgid ""
"Amanda and everybody says Quetzalcoatl is a\n"
"quetzal in the form of a god.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/10
msgid ""
"But there's no way anybody'd mistake a snake for\n"
"a bird,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/11
msgid ""
"I think the legend of Quetzalcoatl came first.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/12
msgid ""
"Somebody saw it and adopted it as their god,\n"
"before they saw the quetzal.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/13
msgid ""
"After that, somebody saw a bird that looked like\n"
"the image of the god,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/14
msgid ""
"and so they named it \"quetzal.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/15
msgid ""
"You mean it happened the other way around?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/16
msgid ""
"If you ask me, the quetzalcoatl was probably a\n"
"pterosaur that survived.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/17
msgid ""
"I mean, it's got wings, and it's a reptile, so it\n"
"probably looks kind of like a snake, right?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/18
msgid ""
"Pterosaurs live on in Africa even today. They're\n"
"called the Kongamato and the Olitiau.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/19
msgid ""
"So it makes sense that there'd be pterosaurs on\n"
"the American continent, too,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/20
msgid ""
"and that they survived until the Mayan and Aztec\n"
"eras.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/21
msgid ""
"Lucky for us they're not still around today.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/22
msgid ""
"Who says they aren't? The dinosaurs supposedly\n"
"died out 65 million years ago,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/23
msgid ""
"and the Aztec civilization only arose about 600\n"
"years ago.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/211/0xd3750/24
msgid ""
"If they managed to survive 65 million years, surely\n"
"they couldn't be wiped out in 600.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 445..1922
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/0
msgid ""
"A base disguised as a mine? We never made it\n"
"that far.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 1964..3162
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/1
msgid ""
"I don't know what kind of place it is, but you'd\n"
"better be careful - just in case.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 3190..3496
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/2
msgid ""
"I plan to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 3510..5196
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/3
msgid ""
"I've heard that the American army keeps dead alien\n"
"bodies and UFOs in secret bases.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 5461..5726
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/4
msgid ""
"Aliens?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 5726..6325
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/5
msgid ""
"There are billions of stars in space.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 6394..7523
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/6
msgid ""
"You've gotta think that at least a few have\n"
"civilizations more advanced than ours.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 7648..8526
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/7
msgid ""
"I'll bet they visit Earth in UFOs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 8596..9055
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/8
msgid ""
"In 1947,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 9083..10602
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/9
msgid ""
"the army actually announced they'd caught a flying,\n"
"disc-shaped object near Roswell, New Mexico.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 10699..11828
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/10
msgid ""
"Maybe you don't know about it, but those army\n"
"guys, they all know!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 12176..12455
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/11
msgid ""
"You don't say...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 12455..13736
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/12
msgid ""
"Anyway, there's no telling what kind of mystery\n"
"weapons they might have stashed up there.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_000_0
#. timeline 13848..14182
#: codec/1/212/0xd43b0/13
msgid ""
"Watch your back.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/0
msgid ""
"Apparently, UFOs are connected to cattle\n"
"mutilations.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/1
msgid ""
"Cattle mutations?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/2
msgid ""
"Not mutations. Mutilations... It's a word I'd never\n"
"heard before.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/3
msgid ""
"People have been reporting their livestock dying\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/4
msgid ""
"in mysterious ways near the same places where\n"
"UFOs have been sighted.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/5
msgid ""
"They say\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/6
msgid ""
"the bodies are drained of blood and the eyeballs\n"
"and sexual organs are gouged out.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/7
msgid ""
"When you leave a corpse cut open in a field\n"
"somewhere, the ground soaks up the blood.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/8
msgid ""
"Yeah, but supposedly these cows weren't cut up\n"
"by any man-made means.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/9
msgid ""
"Maybe maggots got to 'em?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/10
msgid ""
"In some cases they detected radiation.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/11
msgid ""
"Radiation...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/12
msgid ""
"Even in our own town we had goats that died in\n"
"strange ways.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/13
msgid ""
"Some said they saw a monster\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/14
msgid ""
"- a lizard on two legs, covered in spines from its\n"
"head all the way down its back.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/15
msgid ""
"I wonder if that's what the aliens look like,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/16
msgid ""
"or if it was some pet they brought with them...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/17
msgid ""
"...Either way, it doesn't sound like a very advanced\n"
"civilization to me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/18
msgid ""
"If you see one, tell it I said \"hi!\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/212/0xd4880/19
msgid ""
"Sure... if it speaks human.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 459..1532
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/0
msgid ""
"You wanna know something? I once met an alien\n"
"cat.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 1546..2229
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/1
msgid ""
"An alien... cat?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 2243..3051
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/2
msgid ""
"Yep. It was dark out so I couldn't see too well,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 3120..3956
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/3
msgid ""
"but it was a cat with a huge long tail.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 3998..4500
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/4
msgid ""
"Its eyes shined in the dark, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 4513..4987
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/5
msgid ""
"Most cats' eyes do...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 5001..6854
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/6
msgid ""
"At first I thought it was a regular cat. But then it\n"
"started talking to me - inside my head.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 6868..7230
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/7
msgid ""
"...Inside your head?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 7230..8345
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/8
msgid ""
"He said his name was Altargozo Elbakki Munyudar.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 8400..9682
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/9
msgid ""
"He'd come to Earth from the Andromeda Galaxy to\n"
"check out Earth's nuclear weapons...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 9724..10992
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/10
msgid ""
"The Andromeda Galaxy... Mankind's barely made it\n"
"to the moon.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 11089..11702
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/11
msgid ""
"We couldn't possibly launch nukes that far.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 11716..13054
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/12
msgid ""
"Elbakki said he was watching over us - to make\n"
"sure we don't destroy ourselves with nukes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 13123..14113
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/13
msgid ""
"Until the day we humans are ready to join the\n"
"Space Federation...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 14489..15659
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/14
msgid ""
"...It's a shame. This is supposed to be the era of\n"
"Détente,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 15729..16899
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/15
msgid ""
"and still we've got people pulling stunts like\n"
"bringing nukes into peaceful countries.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 16941..18111
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/16
msgid ""
"If something ever went wrong and set off a chain\n"
"reaction of retaliation...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0100_030_0
#. timeline 18111..19379
#: codec/1/213/0xd53f0/17
msgid ""
"I know. This planet could destroy itself at anytime.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 459..1393
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/0
msgid ""
"Snake, is it true you took a picture of el colibri?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 1393..1964
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/1
msgid ""
"Yep. Got it right here.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 1978..4026
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/2
msgid ""
"Whoa! It's like an actual UFO! I knew it - los\n"
"yanquis are working with the aliens!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 4221..4973
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/3
msgid ""
"I know it kind of looks that way, but...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 4987..5684
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/4
msgid ""
"Hey Snake, can you make me a copy of that?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 5698..6506
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/5
msgid ""
"I don't see why not. What for?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 6520..7871
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/6
msgid ""
"People pay good money for this stuff. We can use\n"
"it to raise money for MSF.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 7927..9181
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/7
msgid ""
"Ha, sure, kid. You go out and get us a good price\n"
"for it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0110_000_0
#. timeline 9195..10518
#: codec/1/213/0xd5a60/8
msgid ""
"You don't believe me, do you? I'll get the money.\n"
"You'll see!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/0
msgid ""
"Chico. I, uh... I met that talking cat.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/1
msgid ""
"The legendary Trenya? Really?!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/2
msgid ""
"Trenya? Yeah, that's what it called itself. Is it\n"
"famous?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/3
msgid ""
"In certain circles, yeah.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/4
msgid ""
"I'm still having trouble believing it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/5
msgid ""
"I never thought I'd be talking to an animal one day.\n"
"What a world.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/6
msgid ""
"Amazing you could understand its language.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/7
msgid ""
"Picking up the local lingo is one of the basics of\n"
"intelligence work.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/8
msgid ""
"That's what makes you the Boss, Boss! Hey, say\n"
"something in Trenya's language, will you?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/9
msgid ""
"Meow? Meow... Meow meow meow...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/10
msgid ""
"Wow! I have no idea what you're saying!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/11
msgid ""
"...Of course you wouldn't.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/12
msgid ""
"So what did Trenya say?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/13
msgid ""
"It said it would take me to that island you talked\n"
"about.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/14
msgid ""
"Really?! Take me too, Boss! Please, please!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/15
msgid ""
"I know you must be excited, but we don't know\n"
"what's out there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/16
msgid ""
"It could be dangerous. I'll scout it out first.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/17
msgid ""
"No fair!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/18
msgid ""
"Come on, Chico. This isn't as cut and dry as you\n"
"think.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/19
msgid ""
"You can come next time, depending on what I find.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd63b0/20
msgid ""
"I'll take some photos if I get the chance. Sorry,\n"
"kid, but that's life.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/0
msgid ""
"Apparently there are other cats that talk besides\n"
"Trenya on Isla del Monstruo.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/1
msgid ""
"There's more of them?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/2
msgid ""
"Yep. They're called the Felynes, but supposedly\n"
"they don't ever come to Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/3
msgid ""
"You should try talking to them if you spot them.\n"
"Who knows what kinda stuff they have to say.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/4
msgid ""
"Yeah. Just when you think things can't get any\n"
"crazier...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/5
msgid ""
"Also, the Felynes are nice to humans, so you be\n"
"sure and be nice back.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/6
msgid ""
"Don't you go attacking them or anything.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/214/0xd6a70/7
msgid ""
"I would never hurt a defenseless little kitty.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/0
msgid ""
"Tigrex is a wyvern just like Rathalos.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/1
msgid ""
"But it's good at moving around on land, too.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/2
msgid ""
"It can blast you with rocks from a distance, or\n"
"rush at you with incredible speed.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/3
msgid ""
"People have seen it on land?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/4
msgid ""
"Sí.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/5
msgid ""
"It's said that these two lady pirates, Anne and\n"
"Mary, visited Isla del Monstruo.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/6
msgid ""
"It was there that they did battle with Tigrex.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/7
msgid ""
"Anne was quite a marksman, wasn't she?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/8
msgid ""
"Must've been a heck of a battle. I wish I'd been\n"
"there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/9
msgid ""
"You know, I'm not so bad with guns myself...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd71b0/10
msgid ""
"I've already seen how good you are.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/0
msgid ""
"Anne and Mary also saw little dinosaurs running\n"
"around the island.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/1
msgid ""
"Velocipreys?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/2
msgid ""
"Yup. As you'd expect they're very nimble - but no\n"
"match for a firearm.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/3
msgid ""
"You wouldn't want to get surrounded by them,\n"
"though.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/4
msgid ""
"I'll bet. Nobody wants to be outnumbered in battle.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/5
msgid ""
"Right. Your best move would be to make sure they\n"
"cannot encircle you.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/6
msgid ""
"Well, stealth is the basis of all solo sneaking\n"
"missions...\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/7
msgid ""
"While it makes battle tougher,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/8
msgid ""
"working alone has its advantages when it comes to\n"
"infiltration.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/9
msgid ""
"That's what makes you the boss, Boss! You don't\n"
"need any advice from me.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/10
msgid ""
"Not bad for an old-timer, eh Chico?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd7560/11
msgid ""
"Nope. Still, be careful.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/0
msgid ""
"Have you heard the legend about the dinosaur that\n"
"came back to life as a zombie\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/1
msgid ""
"and attacked people?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/2
msgid ""
"Zombie?! You mean the living dead?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/3
msgid ""
"Yeah. Dinosaurs may be extinct,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/4
msgid ""
"but technically it would be possible for one to\n"
"come back to life as a zombie.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/5
msgid ""
"Not so fast. Dinosaurs were real, zombies... not so\n"
"much.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/6
msgid ""
"What are you talking about, Boss!\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/7
msgid ""
"Zombies have been used as slaves on Haitian\n"
"plantations for years.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/8
msgid ""
"In Haiti they've handed down a secret zombie\n"
"powder for generations.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/10
msgid ""
"People from long ago must have used that same\n"
"stuff on dinosaur remains.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/11
msgid ""
"But dinosaurs had been extinct for millions of\n"
"years before the first humans-\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/12
msgid ""
"That hypothesis has to be wrong.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/13
msgid ""
"...In any case, this zombie was incredibly powerful.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/14
msgid ""
"Its name was Gear REX. They say nothing could kill\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/15
msgid ""
"Some say its bodily fluids would burn right through\n"
"your flesh.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/16
msgid ""
"Then the spines that fell off its back would impale\n"
"you,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/17
msgid ""
"the pain made even worse by the deafening roar\n"
"rattling every bone in your body.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/18
msgid ""
"...You sure it wasn't just some really strong\n"
"monster?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/19
msgid ""
"Who knows what kind of dinosaurs were out there.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/20
msgid ""
"We could be talking about something strong\n"
"enough to resist small arms fire.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/21
msgid ""
"Are you afraid of zombies, Boss?\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/22
msgid ""
"...No. I just find the whole thing hard to believe.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/0
msgid ""
"A fantasma is an espiritu that wanders this plane\n"
"instead of going to el Cielo.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/1
msgid ""
"There are different interpretations, of course, but\n"
"that's what I think.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/2
msgid ""
"See, the fantasma has a reason for remaining in\n"
"this world.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/3
msgid ""
"And if that were, say, a deep hatred for someone,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/4
msgid ""
"they just might be capable of inflicting harm on\n"
"that person.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/5
msgid ""
"You probably realize this, but your weapons or\n"
"CQC won't work on fantasma.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/6
msgid ""
"And since they're not physical beings, they can\n"
"pass right through solid objects.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/7
msgid ""
"But, if you can eliminate their reason for remaining\n"
"here,\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/8
msgid ""
"you should be able to help them reach el Cielo.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/9
msgid ""
"People say words can work wonders on fantasma.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/216/0xd81a0/10
msgid ""
"You could try talking to them through CO-OPS\n"
"communication.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 459..1504
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/0
msgid ""
"You can't always see fantasma with your naked eye.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 1518..2967
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/1
msgid ""
"If some unseen presence is making a noise, you\n"
"can be sure one is around.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 2967..3956
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/2
msgid ""
"When that happens, try taking photos in the area.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 3970..4583
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/3
msgid ""
"You should be able to see what's causing it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 4597..5126
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/4
msgid ""
"Why do they show up on photos?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 5168..5739
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/5
msgid ""
"I'm not the one to ask about that, but...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 5753..7537
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/6
msgid ""
"Maybe fantasma are somehow able to deceive our\n"
"minds - on a subconscious level.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 7551..9153
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/7
msgid ""
"They're right there in front of us, but they whisper,\n"
"\"Hey, we're not really here!\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 9153..10616
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/8
msgid ""
"But a camera is a machine, so they can't do\n"
"anything to it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 10616..11466
#: codec/1/216/0xd8610/9
msgid ""
"Yeah, that's it! That's gotta be it!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 445..1337
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/0
msgid ""
"That's a rangefinder camera you have, right, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 1337..2020
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/1
msgid ""
"Mi viejo used to talk about rangefinder cameras,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 2020..3274
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/2
msgid ""
"and how they can focus just as well as any other\n"
"camera, despite their size.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 3315..4193
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/3
msgid ""
"He also said they don't have much picture blur,\n"
"either.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 4207..4834
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/4
msgid ""
"To bring an object into focus,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 4834..5893
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/5
msgid ""
"make sure the two images overlap before taking\n"
"the picture.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 5907..6631
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/6
msgid ""
"But you could probably do that in your sleep,\n"
"couldn't you?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 6631..7871
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/7
msgid ""
"All you need to worry about is making sure your\n"
"subject is in the frame.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_mis_chc0040_000_0
#. timeline 7899..9181
#: codec/1/216/0xd89e0/8
msgid ""
"Remember, Snake, photography is all about timing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 459..891
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/0
msgid ""
"Sorry to hear about your dad.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 905..2229
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/1
msgid ""
"Don't be. He was... He is a guerrilla warrior.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 2326..3134
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/2
msgid ""
"We pledge our lives to our country and its people...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 3190..3705
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/3
msgid ""
"I'm ready to die, too, if I have to.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 3733..3984
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/4
msgid ""
"You sure?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 4054..5600
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/5
msgid ""
"You'd better believe it! Like mi viejo used to say,\n"
"\"Patria o Muerte.\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 5948..6325
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/6
msgid ""
"Che said it first.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 6339..6924
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/7
msgid ""
"My dad used to tell us all kinds of stories.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 7007..7857
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/8
msgid ""
"About General Sandino and his fight against la\n"
"Guardia...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 7927..8470
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/9
msgid ""
"And about my mom before she left us.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 8512..8860
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/10
msgid ""
"You didn't want to go with her?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 8874..10072
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/11
msgid ""
"It's not like that. La revolución comes first, that's all.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 10142..10657
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/12
msgid ""
"You must wish you could see her, though.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 10671..12496
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/13
msgid ""
"I dunno. But I know I'll see her again when this is\n"
"all over. Somehow I just know it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 12566..13890
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/14
msgid ""
"When I do, me and mamá and papá are all going to\n"
"live together again.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 14210..14475
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/15
msgid ""
"At least...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 15241..15631
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/16
msgid ""
"At least, that's what I thought.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_000_0
#. timeline 17512..18529
#: codec/1/217/0xd9190/17
msgid ""
"Hang in there, Chico. Your sister needs you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 459..1880
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/0
msgid ""
"Have you ever heard, \"Shoot, coward, you are only\n"
"going to kill a man\"?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 2256..2716
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/1
msgid ""
"Che's last words.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 2730..3260
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/2
msgid ""
"He'd been captured in Bolivia,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 3315..4207
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/3
msgid ""
"and said it to the soldiers just as they were about\n"
"to execute him.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 4207..5182
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/4
msgid ""
"El Che... He was something, wasn't he?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 5252..6227
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/5
msgid ""
"Coming up with a line like that knowing he was\n"
"about to die.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 6241..6743
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/6
msgid ""
"After the Cuban Revolution,\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 6743..8094
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/7
msgid ""
"Che gave up his position in the new government to\n"
"aide in revolutions in other countries.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 8317..9473
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/8
msgid ""
"He knew he could die at any time, and he was\n"
"ready for it.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 9487..10365
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/9
msgid ""
"Me, I couldn't take even a little torture...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 10407..11661
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/10
msgid ""
"But you've been reborn, as an hombre nuevo.\n"
"Right, Chico?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0020_010_0
#. timeline 11674..11925
#: codec/1/217/0xd9750/11
msgid ""
"Right...\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 445..1253
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/0
msgid ""
"Don't you ever get lonely living away from your\n"
"mom?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 1267..2173
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/1
msgid ""
"Not really. My compas are my family now.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 2270..2786
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/2
msgid ""
"A lot of them are from the same village as me.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 2814..3538
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/3
msgid ""
"So you had plenty of people to take care of you.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 3566..4890
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/4
msgid ""
"Take care of me?! I'm a warrior, like any other\n"
"Sandinista!\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 4987..5809
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/5
msgid ""
"We look out for each other. That is how it works.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 5879..6645
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/6
msgid ""
"Sorry. Guess I misspoke.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 6659..8150
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/7
msgid ""
"Now we're scattered because of that colibri... I\n"
"wonder where everybody went.\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 8345..9724
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/8
msgid ""
"Hey, Snake. If you see any Frente prisoners, please\n"
"you gotta get them out, OK?\n"
msgstr ""

#. speaker 0x0e559953 voice v_bri_chc0030_000_0
#. timeline 9766..10964
#: codec/1/217/0xd9b70/9
msgid ""
"Those guys are solid - every one. You could use\n"
"them in MSF.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/0
msgid ""
"What's with all this sighing? You're not your usual\n"
"self.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/1
msgid ""
"Oh. Snake.\n"
msgstr ""

#: codec/1/218/0xda210/2
msgid ""
"Something on your mind?\n"
